  "worked_solution": "The sixth term is represented by $f(6).$\n\nTo compute $f(6),$ we first need to compute $f(3).$ So, we substitute $n=1$ into the recursive formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+2) & =f(n+1)+f(1) \\\\ f(1+2) & =f(1+1)+f(1) \\\\ f(3) & =f(2)+f(1) \\\\ f(3) & =(-4)+(-1) \\\\ f(3) & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to compute $f(4),$ we substitute $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2+2) & =f(2+1)+f(2) \\\\ f(4) & =f(3)+f(2) \\\\ f(4) & =(-5)+(-1) \\\\ f(4) & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe continue this process to compute $f(5)$ and $f(6)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5) & =f(4)+f(3)=(-6)+(-5)=-11 \\\\ f(6) & =f(5)+f(4)=(-11)+(-6)=-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sixth term of the sequence is $f(6)=-17.$",
